        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm working through the root भञ्ज् (bhañj), a rudhadi parasmaipada verb, checking its conjugated forms like भनक्ति, भङ्क्तः, भञ्जन्ति and the first-person forms भनज्मि, भञ्ज्वः, भञ्ज्मः, noting how the nasal infix behaves in this class.\n\nApplying the rule śnānnalopaḥ (6.4.23), the a of śnam gets deleted before weak terminations, so bhanaj + mas reduces to bhañj + mas, giving the final answer भञ्ज्मः.\n\n",
